1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,453
Merchants lose five dollars thirteen for every dollar of fraud once fees, goods, and labor are counted.

2
00:00:08,453 --> 00:00:14,500
And fifty-eight percent of cardholders never contact the merchant before they dispute.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,500
Response time is the gap.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,593
FirstReply closes it.

5
00:00:18,593 --> 00:00:21,203
A buyer opens help from the store.

6
00:00:21,203 --> 00:00:22,703
Order verified.

7
00:00:22,703 --> 00:00:25,140
She says the package never came.

8
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:29,609
The agent doesn’t guess — it checks live PayPal tracking.

9
00:00:29,609 --> 00:00:31,765
The shipment is stuck on hold.

10
00:00:31,765 --> 00:00:36,156
Within policy, it offers a reship or a refund.

11
00:00:36,156 --> 00:00:37,921
She takes the refund.

12
00:00:37,921 --> 00:00:39,984
Money moves through PayPal.

13
00:00:39,984 --> 00:00:41,687
No dispute filed.

14
00:00:41,687 --> 00:00:42,999
Under a minute.

15
00:00:42,999 --> 00:00:50,328
Every step lands in the merchant console: the chat, the tracking check, the policy decision.

16
00:00:50,328 --> 00:00:54,046
AI judgment — hard-coded money limits.

17
00:00:54,046 --> 00:00:58,937
A Watch-tier buyer’s claim waits in Approvals with the reasons shown.

18
00:00:58,937 --> 00:01:01,203
The merchant stays in control.

19
00:01:01,203 --> 00:01:06,171
A different buyer refuses the fix and files a PayPal dispute.

20
00:01:06,171 --> 00:01:08,218
It shows up in the console.

21
00:01:08,218 --> 00:01:17,703
FirstReply already holds the record — the offer, the decline, the tracking proof — and drafts the evidence package.

22
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:20,703
The merchant reviews and clicks Submit.

23
00:01:20,703 --> 00:01:25,734
The winning case was built while we were still trying to prevent the dispute.

24
00:01:25,734 --> 00:01:33,718
Impact: disputes prevented, dollars saved at the true cost of fraud, minutes instead of days.

25
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:43,874
Built with an LLM agent, the PayPal Agent Toolkit, and a code policy engine — so money never moves because the model said so.

26
00:01:43,874 --> 00:01:46,968
Most tools help merchants win disputes.

27
00:01:46,968 --> 00:01:55,140
FirstReply makes sure the dispute never happens — and if it does, the winning case is already built.

